  "tagline": "Google Research's ANN library using anisotropic quantization; the tech behind Vertex AI and AlloyDB vectors.",
  "description": "ScaNN (Scalable Nearest Neighbors) is Google Research's library for maximum inner product and Euclidean vector search. It combines tree-based partitioning with anisotropic vector quantization, which weights quantization error by its effect on inner-product ranking, and the SOAR technique for better spill-over indexing. It consistently ranks near the top of ANN benchmarks and underlies Google's managed Vertex AI Vector Search and the ScaNN index in AlloyDB. Released for research use via pip on Linux x86 (AVX/FMA) and ARM, it is a library rather than a database.",
